    {
      "id": "holy-week",
      "title": "Holy Week",
      "expands": "Holy Week",
      "note": "From the entry into Jerusalem to the resurrection. Mark counts the days — the fig tree is cursed on the morrow of the entry and found withered the next morning — and Matthew, telling the cleansing of the temple first, is left out there. The Gospels say only that Judas died after his master's condemnation; A. T. Robertson's *Harmony of the Gospels* (1922) sets his death before Jesus is brought to Pilate, and that ordering rests on Robertson alone.",
